A||N||5||FieroJoe||In need of 1st Gen Camaro info!!!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||07-04-2001||11:47 PM||||Specifically, I am having trouble with the headlight doors on a 67 SS.  We have restored this car, and we are now in the process of putting it back together.  I messed with the doors today, and I know that the motors are getting power and all because if the doors are shut, I turn on the lights and they open.  But, the problem is is that they don't close again, until I yank them to the close position.  No motor running or anything.<P>So, if somebody can specifially answer my question here, where else is there to look?  I have tried <A HREF="http://www.f-body.com," TARGET=_blank>www.f-body.com,</A>  but thier forum seems to be small, uninformative, and all about 3rd gen's burning rubber.  I have also tried camaro.com, but that was pretty much the same.<P>So, any hints will be welcome, especially if someone's got a wiring diagram!!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||07-05-2001||02:21 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.camaros.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.camaros.net/</A> <P>You have to register to read the forum, so I can't tell you what kind of info they have, but they they are a 1st gen oriented site.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||07-05-2001||09:51 AM||||I wasn't aware that the sliding doors (part of the Hugger pkg.) were available till '69.?||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||07-05-2001||10:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indiana_resto_guy:<BR><B>I wasn't aware that the sliding doors (part of the Hugger pkg.) were available till '69.?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>67 had electrically operated doors and 68 and 69 had vacumn operated if memory servers me correctly.<P>There is also I think 3 relays 67 models. Check all of them as they have different functions. Is probably that relay that is dead. All are mounted near the headlight region. Can't remember the exact locations.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||07-05-2001||07:53 PM||||The hidden headlights are part of the RS package. Any RS from 67-69 had them.<BR>You could even mix models back them like an RS-SS so that you could get all kinds of goodies.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Hmmm, back when RS actually ment something.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||4
Z||000005||FieroJoe||07-05-2001||10:17 PM||||Yeah, I talked to the owner today and he said he's had the same type of trouble once and a while.  So, that means that I can let him fix it since it wasnt something that we did!<P>Anyways, yes Aus, there are 3 relays and they are hidden on a plate that is inside the fender.  I assume that one of these has to reverse the polarity for the motors, and it is not doing so.<P>Dave Gunsul - We think that this car is a SS clone.  It has a 3 speed auto on the tree, and it's a Berger.  So I think emblems were just swapped and stuff.<P>Thanks for the links though, I'll pass them along to the owner!||||reg||1
